    "https://maritime.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205220": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Operations & Business",
      "description": "SUNY Maritime College\nJob Posting: Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Operations & Business SUNY Maritime College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Operations & Business Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Operations & Business Category: Athletics Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Bronx, NY Posted: Sep 25, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $65,000.00 - $80,000.00 Position ID: 205220 Share About SUNY Maritime College: SUNY Maritime College located on a 55-acre scenic waterfront property on the outskirts of New York City on the Throggs Neck peninsula where the East River meets Long Island Sound. The campus blends the best of two worlds: a comfortable college-town feel with the greatest city in the world. An impressive view of the sound extends toward the North Atlantic, yet only a few miles away are Yankee Stadium and midtown Manhattan. SUNY Maritime offers an array of employment opportunities stemming from entry level to professional positions which encourage growth and development among its employees. Job Description: The Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Operations & Business oversees budget, accounting, student payroll, and purchasing functions of the athletic department; produces bi-monthly budget reports; and ensures compliance with all university rules and regulations related to financial affairs. Assist the Director of Athletics with duties involved in maintaining numerous departmental accounts, focusing on daily purchasing, accounting, and other financial transactions using institutional automated computer systems. Manage and track binding contracts for varsity athletic programs Assist with all special events, camps and clinics in collaboration with Conference Services and coaching staff Supervise and determine work priorities/schedules of work-study students, student assistants and game day workers Prepare and monitor department supplies and inventory Administer/compile end of season surveys Update handbooks and policy manuals annually Manage payments of all officials Maintain a working copy calendar of department events and schedule game day coverage Coordinate all transportation needs for varsity and club teams with the appropriate coach and/or administrator Serve as Game Day Administrator for the athletic department Serve as Club Sports Coordinator Assist with fundraising efforts and coordination with the Institutional Advancement team Assist in organizing and running Student-Athlete Advisory Committee meetings and initiatives. Prepare bi-monthly budget reports for coaches and the Athletic Director Oversee the reconciliation of all athletic accounts on a monthly or bi-monthly basis Set up departmental ledgers for all accounts; record revenues, expenditures, and transfers Manage budgets for the purpose of identifying possible problem areas to avoid overdrafts, counseling budget holders on their responsibilities as necessary; consult with the Athletic Director on these matters. Prepare the proposed budget to be submitted to Athletic Director and for approval from College Administration Track and execute all check request forms, cash receipt deposit forms and donation deposit forms Manage Athletic Department Club Sports and Foundation Accounts revenue and expenditures Complete preparation of all travel vouchers, petty cash vouchers, and purchase requisitions/orders Complete all cash advance requests and handle all reimbursement requests Oversee the hourly allocations of the sports medicine staff as outlined in the budget Manage and oversee the athletics department and coaches procurement card process. Manage student appointments and facilitate bi-weekly approval of student payroll to ensure timely processing of hours worked Prepare and process all department purchase orders and bids according to university regulations, review bids and recommend awards in conjunction with the College Business Office and work directly with vendors on specifications and delivery arrangements Approve all invoices for payment Authorize and supervise all university deposits, assigning revenue codes for entry fees, ticket sales, advertising income, program sales, and other financial transactions as required Conform to the highest standards of professional conduct regarding compliance with department and institutional policies and procedures and adherence to the rules and regulations of athletic governance organizations of which the institution is a member Contribute to the maintenance of good working relationships with all staff, student-athletes, and external constituents through (a) a positive and constructive approach to all tasks, (b) respect for the competencies of others, and (c) appropriate conflict resolution behavior Directly supervises:  Student employees and game day staff Specific Duties and Responsibilities Include: Administrative Support: Fundraising Activities Issues with student-athlete well being Special Events Responsible for attendance at all mandatory Athletic staff meetings Home event game day supervision as assigned by the Athletic Director Requirements: Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, Sports Management or related degree One to three years of experience as a business manager Have knowledge of NCAA Division III rules Certified in First Aid, AED, and CPR currently Excellent interpersonal, teaching and communication skills are essential Possession of a valid Driver's License. Must have a motor vehicle record which is free from major violations or a pattern of repeat violation. Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree in Accounting, Finance, Sports Management or related degree Three to five years of experience in educational, governmental, or commercial accounting/finance. NCAA game day management experience Additional Information: Classification/Salary Range : The Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Operations & Business is a UUP position.  The anticipated salary range for the position is $65,000 - $80,000 annually, with an outstanding benefits package (for more information, please see the UUP Benefit Summary ). Review of applications to commence immediately and conclude when the position is filled. Special Notes: This is a full-time calendar year appointment UUP Position.  Fair Labor Standard Acts (FLSA) Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA.  Internal and external search to occur simultaneously. Budget Title: Staff Assistant Local Title:   Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Operations & Business Line #: 00324 SUNY Maritime College is an Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disabled/Affirmative Action employer, committed to recruiting, supporting and fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff and students. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, or protected veteran status and will not be discriminated against on the basis of disability. For our full non-discrimination statement, see: http://www.sunymaritime.edu/affirmative-action . SUNY Maritime College is committed to maintaining a safe environment for its students, faculty, staff, volunteers and the general public that use our facilities. Therefore, in order to ensure the hiring of employees of the highest integrity and to maintain a safe campus community, SUNY Maritime College will conduct pre-employment background investigations on all individuals for whom employment is to be offered. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (718) 409-7305. It can also be viewed online by selecting University Police > Safety Information > Clery Safety Report (Annual Security & File Safety). Application Instructions: Persons interested in the above position should apply online. Please submit: Cover letter Resume/CV Statement addressing how past and/or potential contributions to diversity, equity, and inclusion will advance Maritime's commitment to inclusive excellence Names and contact information of three professional references Returning Applicants - Login to your SUNY Maritime Careers Account to check your completed application, check/edit your profile or to upload additional documents. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Maritime College 6 Pennyfield Avenue, Bronx, NY 10465"
    },
    "https://maritime.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205226": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering",
      "description": "SUNY Maritime College\nJob Posting: Assistant or Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering SUNY Maritime College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant or Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant or Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering Category: Faculty Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Engineering Locations: Bronx, NY Posted: Sep 29, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $85,000.00 - $100,000.00 Position ID: 205226 Share About SUNY Maritime College: SUNY Maritime College located on a 55-acre scenic waterfront property on the outskirts of New York City on the Throggs Neck peninsula where the East River meets Long Island Sound. The campus blends the best of two worlds: a comfortable college-town feel with the greatest city in the world. An impressive view of the sound extends toward the North Atlantic, yet only a few miles away are Yankee Stadium and midtown Manhattan. SUNY Maritime offers an array of employment opportunities stemming from entry level to professional positions which encourage growth and development among its employees. Job Description: The Engineering Department at SUNY Maritime College invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering. This is a 10-month academic-year appointment and may be eligible for either a non-tenure-track Lecturer or tenure-track Assistant Professor appointment, depending on the candidate's qualifications. SUNY Maritime College's Electrical Engineering program is accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET and has a strong focus on electrical power engineering. The program prepares students to design, service, and operate electrical and electrical power systems, with applications in maritime, transportation-; energy, and industrial environments. Students receive a strong foundation in electrical engineering theory together with extensive hands-on laboratory and practical experience. We welcome applications from candidates with expertise in electrical engineering and particularly encourage candidates with experience in electrical power engineering to apply. Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to: Teach and develop undergraduate courses in electrical engineering, with particular emphasis on electrical power engineering, including areas such as electrical power systems, electric machines, renewable energy, signals and systems, etc. Teach and develop hands-on electrical engineering laboratory courses using contemporary equipment, instrumentation, simulation, and analysis tools. Advise and mentor undergraduate students and support their academic, professional, and career development.  Participate in projects design, undergraduate research, internship, and other student-learning activities. Establish and maintain relationships with industry, maritime organizations, professional societies, and SUNY System to enhance student learning and professional opportunities. Conduct research, applied research, or scholarly/professional activities appropriate to the candidate1s appointment Participate in ABET assessment and continuous improvement activities. Contribute to departmental and college service, including committee work, student recruitment, outreach, and other activities supporting the Electrical Engineering Program. Contribute to a just, inclusive, and supportive educational environment that enables students from diverse backgrounds to achieve their full potential. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Candidates should possess most, if not all, of the following qualifications: An advanced degree in Electrical Engineering or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated ability or potential to teach and develop undergraduate electrical engineering courses. Demonstrated ability or potential to teach laboratory-based and hands-on engineering courses. Demonstrated ability or potential to advise and mentor undergraduate students. Demonstrated ability or potential to conduct research, applied research, or professional engineering activities. A commitment to departmental and college service. A commitment to student recruitment, outreach, and engagement with the engineering and maritime communities. For appointment at the Assistant Professor level, a Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering or a closely related discipline is required, or there must be a reasonable expectation of timely completion of the Ph.D. Highly qualified candidates may be considered for a non-tenure-track Lecturer appointment. Candidates with a master's degree, professional engineering licensure, or significant relevant industrial experience are encouraged to apply. Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to candidates with expertise or professional experience in one or more of the following areas: Electrical Power Engineering and Power Systems Renewable Energy and Energy Storage Electric Machines and Drives Signals and Systems Maritime, transportation, or industrial electrical applications Experience with hands-on engineering education, undergraduate research, industry collaboration, or professional engineering practice is highly desirable. Additional Information: Classification/Salary Range : The Assistant or Associate Professor position is a tenure-track, academic year appointment United University Professions (UUP) position. The anticipated salary range for the position is $85,000 - $100,000 annually. Appointments will be for a fixed term of one or two years, with one-to three-year extensions possible by mutual consent. Compensation includes a full benefits package in accordance with the contract between the State University of New York and United University Professionals, and includes an outstanding benefits package. Salary will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. For additional information, please see the UUP Benefits Summary Review of applications to commence immediately and conclude when the position is filled. Special Notes: This is a 10- Month appointment UUP position. Fair Labor Standard Acts (FLSA) Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. Internal and external search to occur simultaneously. Budget Title: Assistant Professor 10 Month or Associate Professor 10 Month Local Title: Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering or Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering Full-time position is available starting Fall 2027 SUNY Maritime College is an Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disabled/Affirmative Action employer, committed to recruiting, supporting and fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff and students. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, or protected veteran status and will not be discriminated against on the basis of disability. For our full non-discrimination statement, see: http://www.sunymaritime.edu/affirmative-action . SUNY Maritime College is committed to maintaining a safe environment for its students, faculty, staff, volunteers and the general public that use our facilities. Therefore, in order to ensure the hiring of employees of the highest integrity and to maintain a safe campus community, SUNY Maritime College will conduct pre-employment background investigations on all individuals for whom employment is to be offered. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (718) 409-7305. It can also be viewed online by selecting University Police > Safety Information > Clery Safety Report (Annual Security & File Safety). Application Instructions: Persons interested in the above position should apply online. Please submit: Cover letter Resume/CV Statement addressing how past and/or potential contributions to diversity, equity, and inclusion will advance Maritime's commitment to inclusive excellence Names and contact information of three professional references Returning Applicants - Login to your SUNY Maritime Careers Account to check your completed application, check/edit your profile or to upload additional documents. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Maritime College 6 Pennyfield Avenue, Bronx, NY 10465"
    },
    "https://maritime.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205222": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "SUNY Maritime College\nJob Posting: Assistant or Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering SUNY Maritime College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant or Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant or Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering Category: Faculty Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Engineering Locations: Bronx, NY Posted: Sep 29, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $90,000.00 - $115,000.00 Position ID: 205222 Share About SUNY Maritime College: SUNY Maritime College located on a 55-acre scenic waterfront property on the outskirts of New York City on the Throggs Neck peninsula where the East River meets Long Island Sound. The campus blends the best of two worlds: a comfortable college-town feel with the greatest city in the world. An impressive view of the sound extends toward the North Atlantic, yet only a few miles away are Yankee Stadium and midtown Manhattan. SUNY Maritime offers an array of employment opportunities stemming from entry level to professional positions which encourage growth and development among its employees. Job Description: The Engineering Department at Maritime College, State University of New York is seeking to fill a mechanical engineering faculty position. The Assistant or Associate Professor position will be a tenure-track, academic year appointment. The Maritime College mechanical engineering program is accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET and is focused on applied mechanics. The successful candidate must demonstrate the ability to teach core engineering courses and applied mechanics courses for mechanical engineering majors in a collaborative, team-based environment. Experience with first-year introductory engineering courses is also desirable. Faculty will be encouraged to conduct applied research in engineering or other areas of scholarship. SUNY Maritime College is committed to further strengthening its inclusive campus community, one that comprises a diverse faculty, student body, and staff. Maritime College actively seeks applications from women, veterans, individuals with a disability, and members of underrepresented groups. Requirements: Required Qualifications A Ph.D. in mechanical engineering or a closely allied field (e.g., Marine Engineering, Naval Architecture) together with previous academic or industrial experience is required for the Associate Professor Rank. A reasonable expectation of timely completion of a Ph.D. is required for the Assistant Professor Rank. Practical industrial or research experience is highly desirable, particularly marine industrial experience. Holding a Professional Engineering license or a USCG license as a marine engineering officer is also highly desirable. Highly qualified individuals not holding a Ph.D. may be considered for a full-time, non-tenure track Lecturer position Additional Information: Classification/Salary Range : The Assistant or Associate Professor position is a tenure-track, academic year appointment United University Professions (UUP) position.The anticipated salary range for the position is $90,000.00 to $115,000.00 annually,  Appointments will be for a fixed term of one or two years, with one-to three-year extensions possible by mutual consent. Compensation includes a full benefits package in accordance with the contract between the State University of New York and United University Professionals, and includes an outstanding benefits package. Salary will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. For additional information, please see the UUP Benefits Summary : Review of applications to commence immediately and conclude when the position is filled. Special Notes: This is a Full- Time Academic Year UUP position. Fair Labor Standard Acts (FLSA) Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. Internal and external search to occur simultaneously. Budget Title: Assistant Professor 10 Month or Associate Professor 10 Month Local Title: Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering or Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering Full-time position is available starting Fall 2027 SUNY Maritime College is an Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disabled/Affirmative Action employer, committed to recruiting, supporting and fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff and students. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, or protected veteran status and will not be discriminated against on the basis of disability. For our full non-discrimination statement, see: http://www.sunymaritime.edu/affirmative-action . SUNY Maritime College is committed to maintaining a safe environment for its students, faculty, staff, volunteers and the general public that use our facilities. Therefore, in order to ensure the hiring of employees of the highest integrity and to maintain a safe campus community, SUNY Maritime College will conduct pre-employment background investigations on all individuals for whom employment is to be offered. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (718) 409-7305. It can also be viewed online by selecting University Police > Safety Information > Clery Safety Report (Annual Security & File Safety). Application Instructions: Persons interested in the above position should apply online. Please submit: Cover letter Resume/CV Statement addressing how past and/or potential contributions to diversity, equity, and inclusion will advance Maritime's commitment to inclusive excellence Names and contact information of three professional references Returning Applicants - Login to your SUNY Maritime Careers Account to check your completed application, check/edit your profile or to upload additional documents. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Maritime College 6 Pennyfield Avenue, Bronx, NY 10465"
    },
    "https://maritime.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205259": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Marine Transportation",
      "description": "SUNY Maritime College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Marine Transportation SUNY Maritime College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Marine Transportation Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Marine Transportation Category: Faculty Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Marine Transportation Locations: Bronx, NY Posted: Sep 28, 2026 Closes: Oct 28, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $70,245.00 - $70,245.00 Position ID: 205259 Share About SUNY Maritime College: SUNY Maritime College located on a 55-acre scenic waterfront property on the outskirts of New York City on the Throggs Neck peninsula where the East River meets Long Island Sound. The campus blends the best of two worlds: a comfortable college-town feel with the greatest city in the world. An impressive view of the sound extends toward the North Atlantic, yet only a few miles away are Yankee Stadium and midtown Manhattan. SUNY Maritime offers an array of employment opportunities stemming from entry level to professional positions which encourage growth and development among its employees. Job Description: The Assistant Professor of Marine Transportation provides specialized academic, professional, and experiential instruction in marine transportation, navigation, shipboard operations, maritime safety, vessel management, and related areas of professional maritime education. The position supports the education and professional development of students preparing for careers as U.S. Coast Guard-licensed deck officers and other maritime professionals. Instruction integrates academic theory with contemporary commercial maritime practice, professional credentialing requirements, navigation and bridge technology, maritime simulation, operational decision-making, and shipboard training. The faculty member is expected to teach across multiple areas of the Marine Transportation curriculum; participate in practical, simulator-based, and shipboard instruction; contribute to curriculum development and assessment; advise students; participate in departmental and College service; maintain professional engagement with the maritime industry; and participate in Summer Sea Term training as required by the Department. Duties and Responsibilities The incumbent will be assigned Marine Transportation, Navigation, Nautical Operations, Maritime Technology, and related courses according to the instructional needs of the Department and the faculty member's professional qualifications and experience. Teaching assignments may include, but are not limited to: Vessel Operations and Seamanship Terrestrial and Celestial Navigation Electronic Navigation and Bridge Systems Rules of the Road and Collision Avoidance Ship Handling and Bridge Resource Management Cargo Operations and Vessel Management Maritime Safety and Emergency Procedures Stability and Ship Construction Maritime Regulation and Professional Practice Survival Craft and practical seamanship U.S. Coast Guard License Examination Preparation Maritime Simulation and Simulator Operations The faculty member will: Prepare and deliver classroom, laboratory, simulator, shipboard, and experiential instruction in Marine Transportation and related professional maritime subjects. Develop, administer, and evaluate examinations, practical assessments, simulator exercises, projects, and other appropriate measures of student competency. Develop and maintain instructional materials, syllabi, laboratory exercises, simulator scenarios, assessments, and course content consistent with College requirements and applicable professional maritime standards. Provide theoretical and practical instruction in navigation, vessel operations, bridge management, maritime safety, cargo operations, and other deck-officer competencies. Design and deliver realistic simulator-based scenarios involving navigation, collision avoidance, bridge resource management, vessel operations, emergency response, and professional decision-making. Integrate contemporary maritime technologies and professional practices into instruction, including electronic navigation systems, bridge equipment, automation, decision-support systems, and emerging maritime technologies. Provide instruction and assessment related to professional maritime credentialing and preparation for U.S. Coast Guard deck-officer examinations and qualifications. Participate in shipboard and experiential education, which may include instruction aboard the Training Ship, operation and command of small vessels, pier-side instruction, swimming-pool exercises, firefighting-field activities, and other hands-on professional training environments. Advise and mentor students pursuing professional maritime careers and provide academic and professional guidance related to licensure, shipboard employment, and maritime career development. Participate in curriculum review, development, assessment, accreditation, and continuous improvement of Marine Transportation and maritime license programs. Participate in departmental and College governance, committees, recruitment, outreach, faculty development, and other institutional-service activities. Maintain professional engagement with the maritime industry, regulatory agencies, professional organizations, maritime educational institutions, and other appropriate stakeholders. Conduct and disseminate scholarly, professional, or applied work in areas related to marine transportation, navigation, maritime education and training, maritime safety, ship operations, simulation, or related areas. Remain current with changes in professional maritime practice, regulatory requirements, vessel operations, navigation technology, maritime simulation, and maritime education and training. Perform other academic, instructional, professional, and institutional duties normally associated with a full-time faculty appointment in Marine Transportation. Summer Sea Term Requirement Participation in two out of three Summer Sea Terms on an annual basis is expected, based upon departmental and institutional requirements. Summer Sea Term service involves professional shipboard training and supervision of cadets in navigation, bridge operations, seamanship, maritime safety, vessel operations, and related deck-training activities. Requirements: Bachelor's degree in Marine Transportation, Nautical Science, Maritime Studies, Transportation, or a closely related field. Substantial progressively responsible professional maritime experience involving shipboard navigation, vessel operations, marine transportation, maritime safety, cargo operations, or related professional maritime activities. Professional deck-officer credential or internationally recognized equivalent demonstrating advanced operational maritime expertise. Demonstrated professional or academic expertise in one or more of the following: Navigation and bridge operations; Shipboard operations and vessel management; Cargo operations; Bridge Resource Management; Maritime simulation; Maritime safety and regulatory compliance; or Electronic navigation and bridge systems. Demonstrated ability to teach both theoretical and practical components of professional maritime education. Additional Information: Classification: The anticipated salary range is $70,245 annually and includes an outstanding benefits package (for more information, please see the UUP Full-Time Benefits -at-a-Glance). Salary will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. Review of applications will commence immediately and conclude when the position is filled. Special Notes: Fair Labor Standard Acts (FLSA) Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. Internal and external searches to occur simultaneously. Budget Title: Assistant Professor 10 Month Local Title: Assistant Professor 10 Month SUNY Maritime College is an Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disabled/Affirmative Action employer, committed to recruiting, supporting and fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff and students. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, or protected veteran status and will not be discriminated against on the basis of disability. For our full non-discrimination statement, see: http://www.sunymaritime.edu/affirmative-action . SUNY Maritime College is committed to maintaining a safe environment for its students, faculty, staff, volunteers and the general public that use our facilities. Therefore, in order to ensure the hiring of employees of the highest integrity and to maintain a safe campus community, SUNY Maritime College will conduct pre-employment background investigations on all individuals for whom employment is to be offered. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (718) 409-7305. It can also be viewed online by selecting University Police > Safety Information > Clery Safety Report (Annual Security & File Safety). Application Instructions: Persons interested in the above position should apply online. Please submit: Cover letter Resume/CV Statement addressing how past and/or potential contributions to diversity, equity, and inclusion will advance Maritime's commitment to inclusive excellence Names and contact information of three professional references Returning Applicants - Login to your SUNY Maritime Careers Account to check your completed application, check/edit your profile or to upload additional documents. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Maritime College 6 Pennyfield Avenue, Bronx, NY 10465"
    }
